I successfully completed the Cyber Kill Chain room on TryHackMe, where I explored the stages of a cyber attack and learned how 
security teams use the Cyber Kill Chain framework to detect, analyze, and prevent network intrusions.

This room provided practical insight into how adversaries operate throughout the attack lifecycle and how defenders can identify 
malicious activity at each stage before attackers achieve their objectives.

## Overview

The Cyber Kill Chain, developed by Lockheed Martin, is a cybersecurity framework used to understand and disrupt attacker operations by
breaking down attacks into sequential phases.

The module focused on understanding how attackers progress from initial reconnaissance to achieving their objectives, and how defenders 
can implement detection and mitigation strategies throughout the intrusion lifecycle.

