## Cyber Kill Chain Phases Studied

  -Reconnaissance – Gathering information about the target
  -Weaponization – Creating malicious payloads and attack tools
  -Delivery – Transmitting malware to the target
  -Exploitation – Triggering vulnerabilities for execution
  -Installation – Establishing persistence on the victim system
  -Command & Control (C2) – Maintaining communication with compromised systems
  -Actions on Objectives – Achieving attacker goals such as data theft or system compromise

